[[:db/retract 17592186180174 :question/answer-fields 17592186178588] {:db/id 17592186179728 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b73ad7ec-dc24-5c99-a917-9ce5919adbcd" "question-36f8b820-02e2-5d5e-8155-bd2e7c9da1db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179674 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4ee6b1fc-a5dc-5685-b3c9-ad25e0e1efc1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179673 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-26043436-d017-5e07-ac9c-a4df40dc0429" "question-228970be-ca08-547c-9937-b7e76a0b4145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b73ad7ec-dc24-5c99-a917-9ce5919adbcd" :question/id #uuid "b73ad7ec-dc24-5c99-a917-9ce5919adbcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-90714" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{FG}$ traversed from the point $F(1,0)$ to the point $G(2,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-xy\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=i$ and $b=2\\,i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =i+t(2\\,i+3\\,j-i) \\\\  & =i+t(i+3\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+t)\\,i+3t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=1+t$ and $y(t)=3t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+3\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-xy\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+t)\\cdot 1-(1+t)\\cdot 3t\\cdot 3\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}1-8t-9{t}^{2}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[t-4{t}^{2}-3{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[1-4(1)^{2}-3(1)^{3}]-[0] \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b523b71f-1a4d-563c-8ba4-de711d207cf0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b523b71f-1a4d-563c-8ba4-de711d207cf0" :answer-field/id #uuid "b523b71f-1a4d-563c-8ba4-de711d207cf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-38c233c1-8522-530d-9bbc-48e152799452" :answer-field/choices ["answer-38c233c1-8522-530d-9bbc-48e152799452" "answer-29488f70-3dff-5945-99fa-114e41ce2085" "answer-d6e2e962-8b22-57c7-9fde-b02c03d0533e" "answer-e3ac4b86-8657-5c33-ab2c-ac749e9ddbc9" "answer-794f752f-1659-5318-a69d-58c5a353960e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38c233c1-8522-530d-9bbc-48e152799452" :answer/id #uuid "38c233c1-8522-530d-9bbc-48e152799452" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29488f70-3dff-5945-99fa-114e41ce2085" :answer/id #uuid "29488f70-3dff-5945-99fa-114e41ce2085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6e2e962-8b22-57c7-9fde-b02c03d0533e" :answer/id #uuid "d6e2e962-8b22-57c7-9fde-b02c03d0533e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3ac4b86-8657-5c33-ab2c-ac749e9ddbc9" :answer/id #uuid "e3ac4b86-8657-5c33-ab2c-ac749e9ddbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-794f752f-1659-5318-a69d-58c5a353960e" :answer/id #uuid "794f752f-1659-5318-a69d-58c5a353960e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-36f8b820-02e2-5d5e-8155-bd2e7c9da1db" :question/id #uuid "36f8b820-02e2-5d5e-8155-bd2e7c9da1db" :question/math-academy-id "q-124660" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to the point $B(1,1),$ then ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi y\\,dx-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=0\\,i+0\\,j$ and $b=i+j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =0\\,i+0\\,j+t(i+j-(0\\,i+0\\,j)) \\\\  & =t\\,i+t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=t$ and $y(t)=t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi y\\,dx-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\cdot 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t}{\\pi }-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t}{\\pi }]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[-1+0-1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79e92368-7b49-5e53-95cb-a87e9c528421"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79e92368-7b49-5e53-95cb-a87e9c528421" :answer-field/id #uuid "79e92368-7b49-5e53-95cb-a87e9c528421" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f77ceb7-6be8-5d0b-93e7-60790b6d14db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-65db0f0e-cfd6-52b8-9117-b967fb489769" "answer-488a4e09-5667-54f6-ad88-5c61e9a4ef4c" "answer-2f77ceb7-6be8-5d0b-93e7-60790b6d14db" "answer-9b98bb58-d459-5b8d-8729-a3f1ab440861" "answer-8b52cac3-7234-5848-87cf-921935519eb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65db0f0e-cfd6-52b8-9117-b967fb489769" :answer/id #uuid "65db0f0e-cfd6-52b8-9117-b967fb489769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-488a4e09-5667-54f6-ad88-5c61e9a4ef4c" :answer/id #uuid "488a4e09-5667-54f6-ad88-5c61e9a4ef4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f77ceb7-6be8-5d0b-93e7-60790b6d14db" :answer/id #uuid "2f77ceb7-6be8-5d0b-93e7-60790b6d14db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b98bb58-d459-5b8d-8729-a3f1ab440861" :answer/id #uuid "9b98bb58-d459-5b8d-8729-a3f1ab440861" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b52cac3-7234-5848-87cf-921935519eb4" :answer/id #uuid "8b52cac3-7234-5848-87cf-921935519eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4ee6b1fc-a5dc-5685-b3c9-ad25e0e1efc1" :question/id #uuid "4ee6b1fc-a5dc-5685-b3c9-ad25e0e1efc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-124666" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the graph $y={x}^{2}-1$ traversed from the point $P(1,0)$ to point $Q(2,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+x\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y={x}^{2}-1.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+({t}^{2}-1)\\,j,\\,t\\in [1,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+1+2{t}^{2}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{4}+1\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}+t]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{2}^{5}}{5}+2]-[\\frac{{1}^{5}}{5}+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}+2-\\frac{1}{5}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac11d5c1-82f1-564e-be01-8e20a8e6d4bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac11d5c1-82f1-564e-be01-8e20a8e6d4bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac11d5c1-82f1-564e-be01-8e20a8e6d4bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff788f7f-efa0-5800-af8c-7f4c47429255" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7872d0b7-7e4c-5866-a2c5-fa62a0852ac3" "answer-5b61e1f7-a8be-5897-ab62-f5700cfc5da5" "answer-3341cdec-88e2-5336-a6c4-1be4742e22df" "answer-225888f9-79d1-51ec-b69e-df715e48a48c" "answer-ff788f7f-efa0-5800-af8c-7f4c47429255"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7872d0b7-7e4c-5866-a2c5-fa62a0852ac3" :answer/id #uuid "7872d0b7-7e4c-5866-a2c5-fa62a0852ac3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b61e1f7-a8be-5897-ab62-f5700cfc5da5" :answer/id #uuid "5b61e1f7-a8be-5897-ab62-f5700cfc5da5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3341cdec-88e2-5336-a6c4-1be4742e22df" :answer/id #uuid "3341cdec-88e2-5336-a6c4-1be4742e22df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-225888f9-79d1-51ec-b69e-df715e48a48c" :answer/id #uuid "225888f9-79d1-51ec-b69e-df715e48a48c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff788f7f-efa0-5800-af8c-7f4c47429255" :answer/id #uuid "ff788f7f-efa0-5800-af8c-7f4c47429255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180174 :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y={x}^{2}$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to point $B(2,4),$ then ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+y\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y={x}^{2}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+y\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\cdot 1+{t}^{2}\\cdot 2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}t+2{t}^{3}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =2+8 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-55008b23-7b99-5d0d-87f9-a75bcea2d1c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-55008b23-7b99-5d0d-87f9-a75bcea2d1c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "55008b23-7b99-5d0d-87f9-a75bcea2d1c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9c20e31-578e-5df9-8b7f-fd828cbb1b39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9c20e31-578e-5df9-8b7f-fd828cbb1b39" "answer-7cadedbb-d8e2-5bdf-97a6-9ad1eb1ceece" "answer-dc50983f-8d67-57c5-a859-8dc7f564511a" "answer-49e57c7d-ef79-5439-be59-40bbdc9b3e0d" "answer-c58f6ab5-55eb-56af-a44a-0c359a236b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9c20e31-578e-5df9-8b7f-fd828cbb1b39" :answer/id #uuid "e9c20e31-578e-5df9-8b7f-fd828cbb1b39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cadedbb-d8e2-5bdf-97a6-9ad1eb1ceece" :answer/id #uuid "7cadedbb-d8e2-5bdf-97a6-9ad1eb1ceece" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc50983f-8d67-57c5-a859-8dc7f564511a" :answer/id #uuid "dc50983f-8d67-57c5-a859-8dc7f564511a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49e57c7d-ef79-5439-be59-40bbdc9b3e0d" :answer/id #uuid "49e57c7d-ef79-5439-be59-40bbdc9b3e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c58f6ab5-55eb-56af-a44a-0c359a236b18" :answer/id #uuid "c58f6ab5-55eb-56af-a44a-0c359a236b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-26043436-d017-5e07-ac9c-a4df40dc0429" :question/id #uuid "26043436-d017-5e07-ac9c-a4df40dc0429" :question/math-academy-id "q-90895" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx-x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(\\sqrt{2},0)$ to the point $B(0,\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the parametrization of the curve $C.$ Since it's a circle if radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin, the curve $C$ can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve we have that $x(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx-x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(y\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}-x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-2{sin}^{2}⁡t-2{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-2[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0] \\\\  & =-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b64329ed-5836-53c3-881a-5ef3bf67996e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b64329ed-5836-53c3-881a-5ef3bf67996e" :answer-field/id #uuid "b64329ed-5836-53c3-881a-5ef3bf67996e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72db92dd-d3bb-5244-9ae0-06d36401d8d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56de169b-e6cc-53f1-9778-d57c45a41155" "answer-72db92dd-d3bb-5244-9ae0-06d36401d8d9" "answer-256764ed-4369-50dc-930e-662876f022a1" "answer-4130f50c-9761-535e-832c-969370eba9c6" "answer-fb33e709-cf30-5cd2-9a8f-17fc862403a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56de169b-e6cc-53f1-9778-d57c45a41155" :answer/id #uuid "56de169b-e6cc-53f1-9778-d57c45a41155" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72db92dd-d3bb-5244-9ae0-06d36401d8d9" :answer/id #uuid "72db92dd-d3bb-5244-9ae0-06d36401d8d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-256764ed-4369-50dc-930e-662876f022a1" :answer/id #uuid "256764ed-4369-50dc-930e-662876f022a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4130f50c-9761-535e-832c-969370eba9c6" :answer/id #uuid "4130f50c-9761-535e-832c-969370eba9c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb33e709-cf30-5cd2-9a8f-17fc862403a2" :answer/id #uuid "fb33e709-cf30-5cd2-9a8f-17fc862403a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-228970be-ca08-547c-9937-b7e76a0b4145" :question/id #uuid "228970be-ca08-547c-9937-b7e76a0b4145" :question/math-academy-id "q-81186" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the parametrization of the curve $C.$ Since it's a circle if radius $2$ centered at the origin, the curve $C$ can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve we have that $x(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}y\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(y\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t{|}_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )] \\\\  & =2(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0df18aab-7e84-55d8-803f-e0704648d1b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0df18aab-7e84-55d8-803f-e0704648d1b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "0df18aab-7e84-55d8-803f-e0704648d1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f548fd7-8b35-5ec3-9cec-fbc79515f307" :answer-field/choices ["answer-910075a4-9923-557c-b9e3-c1e2ff793ed6" "answer-f7735ce7-7b0f-5b5a-82f6-7e753a067e1c" "answer-2f548fd7-8b35-5ec3-9cec-fbc79515f307" "answer-d7d88b10-d2ad-5c06-9db7-9b7365276f6d" "answer-68411306-3576-579b-8a21-34c1ab7c2b84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-910075a4-9923-557c-b9e3-c1e2ff793ed6" :answer/id #uuid "910075a4-9923-557c-b9e3-c1e2ff793ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7735ce7-7b0f-5b5a-82f6-7e753a067e1c" :answer/id #uuid "f7735ce7-7b0f-5b5a-82f6-7e753a067e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f548fd7-8b35-5ec3-9cec-fbc79515f307" :answer/id #uuid "2f548fd7-8b35-5ec3-9cec-fbc79515f307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "a